{
  "format": "flashbeat-score-parity/1",
  "description": "Shared scoring vectors for the Unity <-> Web parity contract (Issue #612, ADR-0028, ADR-0029, ADR-0033, ADR-0035, ADR-0037). Each case is one play of a chart with noteCount notes. scoreV1/scoreV2/scoreV3/scoreV4/scoreV5/scoreV6 are the scores the Unity client computes (Scoring.ScoreV1-equivalent via Judge.ComputeScore, Scoring.ScoreV2, Scoring.ScoreV3/Scoring.ScoreV4/Scoring.ScoreV5/Scoring.ScoreV6 with the case's judgmentsComplete flag). scoreV3Settled/scoreV4Settled/scoreV5Settled/scoreV6Settled are the same play evaluated as a completed submission (judgmentsComplete=true) — identical to the Web computeUnityScoreV3/V4/V5/V6 result and to computeUnityScoreV3/V4/V5/V6 called with judgmentsComplete=true, because a submission always implies judgmentsComplete (perfect+great+bad+miss == noteCount). judgmentsComplete=false cases pin the Issue #618 rule that the full-combo bonus never enters the live in-progress projection. scoreV1/scoreV2 are single-precision emulated exactly like web/routes/api/v1/_score-model.ts (Math.fround); scoreV3/scoreV3Settled/scoreV4/scoreV4Settled/scoreV5/scoreV5Settled/scoreV6/scoreV6Settled use the deterministic integer arithmetic of Issue #631/#736/#797/#825 (v3: exact floor of ratio*1e6/maxRatio; v4: base floor(judgment*1e6/(5N)) + bonus floor(bonusRatio*1e6/maxBonusRatio), each capped at 1,000,000; v5: same two halves but the continuous combo bonus is removed and each milestone crossing pays MilestoneBonusPointsV5=250 ratio points; v6: base floor(judgment*1e6/(5N)) plus the absolute additional score perfect*1000+great*600+bad*200 + comboMilestones*5000 + (judgmentsComplete && miss==0 ? 25000 : 0), whose chart maximum 1,000,000+MaxAdditionalV6(noteCount) grows with the note count — identical on every platform). v3SubmissionChecks are consumed by the Web suite only: they pin the server-side comboMilestones bound checks of scoreSemanticsDiagnostics (no Unity counterpart exists — the client only produces the count).",
